<title>UK: Sears gets shareholder OK to sell Freemans.</title>
<headline>Sears gets shareholder OK to sell Freemans.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Sears Plc said on Friday its shareholders approved the disposal of its Freemans mail order business to Littlewoods.  </p>
<p>Sears announced last month that it agreed to sell Freemans for 367.5 million stg as part of the break-up of its retail empire.</p>
<p>The sale was still conditional upon merger clearance from British and Irish regulatory authorities.</p>
<p>Separately, Sears said it agreed to sell The Source, its home fashion business, to Portugal's Sonae for an undisclosed sum. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
